---
title: Turkish Lamb Pilau
description: Serve up a basmati rice one pot flavoured with cinnamon, mint and apricot, studded with tender lamb
cook time: 30 minutes
author: Good Food team
course: Dinner, Lunch, Main course, Supper
time required: 30 minutes
servings: 4
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/turkish-lamb-pilau
cuisine: Turkish
---

Dry-fry @pine nuts{1/4%cup}(or flaked almonds) in a #large pan{} until lightly toasted, then tip onto a plate. 

Add @olive oil{1%tbsp} to the pan, then fry @onion{1}(halved and sliced)
and @cinnamon sticks{2}(broken in half) together until starting to turn golden. 

Turn up the heat, stir in @lamb neck fillet{1%lb}(cubed), fry until the meat changes colour,
then tip in @basmati rice{8%oz} and cook for ~{1%minute}, stirring all the time. 

Pour in @water{2%cups}(boiling), crumble in @lamb stock cube{1},
add @dried apricots{12}(ready-to-eat), then season to taste. 

Turn the heat down, cover and simmer for ~{12%minutes} until the rice is tender and the stock has been absorbed. 

Toss in the @pine nuts{} and @mint leaves{1/4%cup}(roughly chopped) and serve.

= Nutritional Info (per serving) =
584 calories; 24g fat; 9g saturated fat; 65g carbohydrates; 32g protein; 3g fiber; 1.4mg sodium
